{
	"addonId": "lineMR",
	"displayName": "LINE MR (Line Mai Roo) - LINE for Windows accessibility",
	"URL": "https://github.com/Peetchy/line-mr-for-win/releases/download/v0.5.5/lineMR-0.5.5.nvda-addon",
	"description": "Makes LINE for Windows usable with NVDA: names LINE's unlabeled buttons, text fields and checkboxes, reads chat lists and messages (including what a photo, video, sticker, voice message, file, location or call is), makes every control reachable with Tab, and announces incoming calls. Adds a small accessibility bridge to LINE's folder (LINE's own files are not modified). Recommended: LINE from the Microsoft Store (https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/XPFCC4CD725961).\n\nCommands in LINE: Alt+1 / Alt+2 / Alt+3 friends / chats / add friends tab; Alt+C chat list; Alt+L chat or friend list; Alt+F search field; Alt+M messages of the open chat; Alt+I message input; NVDA+Alt+1 to 9 read a recent message (1 = newest); NVDA+Shift+Control+L bridge status.\nCalls: in LINE, Alt+A answers an incoming call and Alt+D declines it or ends the current call; from any application, NVDA+Shift+Control+A answers and NVDA+Shift+Control+D declines or ends the call.\nKeys in lists: chat list - arrows, Page Up/Down, Home/End browse without opening, Enter opens the chat; messages - Up/Down one message, Page Up/Down a screen, Home oldest loaded (again: older), End newest, Applications key the message's menu.",
	"sha256": "8ebaf99bb00a1cd1d0dd3997f721c134deab47ca66c6524c16a66b89f46262ea",
